We explored two design strategies for incorporating this nonlinear behavior into the optimization.​
Option 1 — Direct Optimization: The nonlinear damper model is embedded directly inside the ODE framework. The optimizer simultaneously tune parameters — K_F, C_F, K_2, K_3 — along with the nonlinear damper parameters: compression damping, asymmetry ratio, and compression and rebound factors. Everything is optimized together.​
Option 2 — Two-Phase Optimization with Curve Fitting: In Phase 1, we optimize only the linear parameters. In Phase 2, we use the velocity time history from Phase 1 to fit the nonlinear damper parameters using a weighted least-squares curve fitting approach. The two phases are sequential.​
